   312	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   313	    """
   314	    Assemble scattered sprites into a directed multi-color relay chain rooted at the yellow anchor.
   315	
   316	    Input structure:
   317	    - bg = black (0). Several colored sprites are scattered without touching.
   318	    - Exactly one anchor sprite contains a yellow (4) rectangle and one output connector pair.
   319	    - Connector pixels come in three family-specific role pairs:
   320	      2->3, 5->6, and 7->8 where the smaller color is an output port and the larger color is the matching input port.
   321	
   322	    Rule:
   323	    - The anchor stays fixed and starts the chain.
   324	    - At each step, only the current tail output pair may be extended, and the next piece must place a matching-family input pair on that exact location.
   325	    - If the piece has another connector pair, that pair becomes the new tail; continue until all pieces are consumed and every connector cell is paired exactly once.
   326	
   327	    Key insight:
   328	    - The open frontier is a single directed colored pair, not an arbitrary open connector. Solving requires tracking three things together: which pair is still open, which role it needs next, and which color family is allowed there.
   329	    """
